  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PMI The Gambia Malaria Elimination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Gambia, The):  PMI&apos;s 2021 - 2026 strategy, End Malaria Faster, envisions a world free of malaria within our generation. Its goals are preventing malaria cases, reducing malaria deaths and illness, and eliminating malaria in PMI partner countries. Over the course of this five year strategy, PMI aims to save lives, reduce health inequities, and improve disease surveillance and global health security. The Gambia became a PMI partner country in FY 2023. .With FY 2024 funding, the PMI Gambia Malaria Elimination Activity (GMEA) will address some unmet needs, including initiating a comprehensive package for malaria case-based surveillance in an elimination area(s), launching a community pilot, facilitating the creation of a new social behavior change (SBC) strategy, technical working group, and SBC activities. The activity will also strengthen cross-border planning, coordination, and data sharing between The Gambia and Senegal...</narrative>
  </description>
